# Virtualenvs and caches -- never committed, always reproducible from pyproject.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# The reconciliation database is a build artefact of `make metrics`.
ledger.db
ledger.db-journal

# Secrets. The classifier reads OPENAI_API_KEY from .env when it is present.
# Nothing here may ever reach the repository.
#
# Ignoring `.env` alone is not enough -- `.env.local`, `.env.production` and a
# stray `key.pem` are the ones that actually get committed by accident. The
# real guard is tests/test_no_secrets.py, which scans every TRACKED file for
# key-shaped strings: an ignore rule only helps when the file is named the way
# you expected, and it does nothing at all about a key pasted into config.py.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# macOS
.DS_Store

# NOTE: data/seed_A/ and data/seed_B/ are deliberately NOT ignored. CI regenerates
# them and asserts `git diff --exit-code -- data/`, which only works if the
# committed copies are there to diff against.

# Working notes for whoever picks the build up next. Local only -- it is scaffolding
# for building the thing, not part of the thing, and it has no reader on GitHub.
HANDOFF.md

# The video script is a recording aid, not a deliverable. The video is.
docs/video-script.md
